{"188036": ".\nfig,\n\nHOUSE OF REPRESENTATIVES\n2 STATE HOUSE STATION AUGUSTA, MAINE 04333-0002\n\n~r\nDaniel J. Ankeles\n\n(207) 227-1400\nTTY3 MAINE RELAY 711\n\n7 Beech Drive\nBrunswick, ME 04011\n\nDaniel.Ankeles@legis|ature.maine.gov\n\nCell Phone: (207) 756-3793\n\nApril 2, 2025\n\nTestimony ofRepresentative Dan Ankeles presenting\nLD 1153, An Act to Change in Statute the Areas Represented by the Members\n\nof the Board of Trustees of the Cross Insurance Arena from Sets of\n\nMunicipalities to the County Commissioner Districts of Cumberland County\n\nBefore the Joint Standing Committee on State and Local Government\nV\n\nSenator Baldacci, Representative Salisbury and honorable members of the Joint Standing Committee on State and Local Govermnent, thank you for the opportunity to come before you\ntoday for the first time. I am Representative Dan Ankeles, and I serve House District 100, which\nis a central slice of Brunswick. I'm here to present LD 1153, An Act to Change in Statute the\nAreas Represented by the Members of the Board of Trustees of the Cross Insurance Arena from Sets of Municipalities to the County Commissioner Districts of Cumberland County.\n\nThis is not officially a \"department bill,\" but I am submitting this measure on behalf of\nCumberland Cotmty government. The title is certainly a mouthful, but the bill itself is a clean and simple fix.\n\nIn Portland, you have the Cross Insurance Arena, which is governed by a county-wide board of trustees. There are five geographic district-level members and two at-large members. The district\nmap for this board is exactly the same as the county commissioner map.\n\nThe only difference is that with this board of trustees district map, each district is statutorily defined as a fixed list of towns and is not actually pegged to the county cormnission districts.\n\nThere's not really any good reason for this, so LD 1153 erases that difference and just pegs the\ntrustee district definitions to the county commission map.\n\nI'll use my own district as an example. Trustee District 3 is statutorily defined as Brunswick, Freeport, Harpswell, Pownal and New Gloucester. If this bill were to pass, Trustee District 3\nwould now be defined as County Commission District 3. The list of towns would go away.\n\nThe benefits are a) a reduction in confusion and b) a guarantee that the arena districts, just like\nthe county commissioner districts, will self-adj ust each time we do a census and draw new maps. Which brings me to c) the second-best part -- you won't ever have to see me come before you\never again.\n\nWell then, you might be wondering, what is the best part? If you guessed \"no fiscal note,\" you win! No one-time money, no ongoing money, no new headcount. If you weren't sold before,\nhopefully those were the magic words that just got you to \"yes.\"\nPm happy to answer questions, but you're probably better off directing your queries to the\nrepresentative from Cumberland County government, who is more familiar with the thought\nprocess behind the bill.\nThank you for the opportunity to testify, and I do hope you'll see fit to advance this bill with a favorable recommendation.\n\nCROSS INSURANCE ARENA TRUSTEES\n\nr;iwz', I\nv<%'\"\"\n\nIEI \"\"`I!`Y \"\n:\\=;=`=\";`\\:\\\"\"\n\n.1\n\n25:2-=�:'V�='==@z:2e' .:=.==vs<w#2\n\n~ 1%;\n\n,�.%1w1i`\n\ng\n7,, _\n*2\n\nI\n\n�\n\n=43;\nI\n41\nFrank CIark\n\n':I\nJon Crimmins\n\nJohn Jamieson\n\nSam Surprise\n\nAT-LARGE\nCounty-wide\nLori Norman\n\nAT-LARGE\nCounty-wide\nSteve Woods\n\nI ,\n\nCOMMISSIONER\n\nCounty-wide\n\nSusan Wiionis\n\n. * \\\n\n.\n\n\\>\\\\\\\n\n~{;s:s:BF1�8iOfl LLl\n\n<\n~\n\n~\n, .\n\n,\n-\n[<7 . � >I 1?;/\"I/_:<I`\n\n~\n\n1�\n\n'~`�$�1rf:I<;'W?~\"~\":�jQ`1\"W\\~X*'6`:w \"M.\n\n~\n\nK\n\n1-�_.�\\_~;\\=mg�;;<;=.:,~;q�;@��,;m,;`,,�;,(/��<�~5gmnw;_~ _.\\;;,1~;M<\\z\\,~u_,\n\n` \\\n\n-~ .`\\\\-\\��&*=->c;�w\" .-�-1'1~>m2m.Wwv;��,u >~,,;r/_�'> ~=2.=,.<\\\" \\~~'m�`=\n\n\\~_}\\1a\n\ni;�~;;1`;;-\n\n1:\n\n:s.\\�' _\\~\